        "status": "not-applicable"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "antony-and-cleopatra/sceneIII_3.6/p@110249",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "CAESAR.\nContemning Rome, he has done all this, and more\nIn Alexandria. Here’s the manner of ’t:\nI’ th’ market-place, on a tribunal silvered,\nCleopatra and himself in chairs of gold\nWere publicly enthroned. At the feet sat\nCaesarion, whom they call my father’s son,\nAnd all the unlawful issue that their lust\nSince then hath made between them. Unto her\nHe gave the stablishment of Egypt; made her\nOf lower Syria, Cyprus, Lydia,\nAbsolute queen.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "antony-and-cleopatra/sceneIII_3.6/p@110249/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "antony-and-cleopatra/sceneIII_3.6/p@110249/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 55,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
